   "notes": [
    "One horizontal stacked bar per model and image setting: 24 bars in six groups of four (no image, LLM caption, direct image, human hint), groups separated by an empty row with an unlabelled tick. Categories are the y tick labels exactly as printed, listed top to bottom ('GeminiAdvanced Web- direct image' is printed without a space before the hyphen). The figure itself prints no title; panel.title is the caption.",
    "Segments are stacked left to right in legend order: Correct, 2OP, EOP, NOP, Error, Incorrect. All six series are given for every bar; a class with no visible segment is 0.0. Every bar starts at 0 and ends at 100 (the x axis runs to 105; axes.x.range is the drawn axis, the tick labels are 0-100).",
    "Correct: the percentage printed inside the green segment (source 'printed'). The measured green length agrees with it within 0.10 points on all 24 bars (rms 0.05).",
    "EOP has the same colour as the plot background (#D3D3D3; the legend swatch and the axes face are pixel-identical), so an EOP segment shows only as a background-coloured gap inside a bar, between the 2OP (or Correct) end and the NOP / Error / Incorrect start. Every such gap is recorded as EOP (confidence 0.9): no other class can be hidden there, and the bar continues to 100 behind it.",
    "Measurement: the PDF's embedded bitmap of page 20 (1019 x 1528 px RGB, lossless; 5.684 px per percentage point). X calibration: least squares through the six tick marks 0-100, px = 349.973 + 5.68388 * value (pixel-edge coordinates); residual at the ticks <= 0.01 px (0.002 points). Segment boundaries read per bar on a pixel row clear of the printed label, anti-aliased boundary pixels split linearly between the two colours. Estimated error of a measured segment: +/- 0.1 points (largest deviation from the count pattern below: 0.11).",
    "Check on the total: the right end of every bar lies inside the pixel column of the 100 gridline (bar end = 100.0 +/- 0.09); the white gridline is drawn over the bars, so the last half pixel is hidden. Incorrect is measured from its left boundary to the calibrated 100 position. Printed Correct plus the five measured classes sum to 100 within 0.10 points for every bar.",
